This seems okay too.

Wait, let me look at the actual crash more carefully. The crash is "Heap-use-after-free READ 8". The crash state is:
```
KArchiveDirectory::addEntry 
KArchive::findOrCreate 
KArchive::findOrCreate
```

So the crash happens when `addEntry` is called from `findOrCreate`. Let me look at `addEntry`:

```cpp
void KArchiveDirectory::addEntry(KArchiveEntry *entry)
{
    if (d->entries.value(entry->name())) {
        qCWarning(KArchiveLog) << "directory " << name()
                    << "has entry" << entry->name() << "already";
        delete entry;
        return;
    }
    d->entries.insert(entry->name(), entry);
}
```

The `d->entries.value(entry->name())` accesses `d` which is the private data of the directory. If the directory has been deleted (use-after-free), then `d` would be invalid.

So the question is: how can a directory be deleted while `findOrCreate` is still using it?

